To fix the error, you should change the return type of the `async fn` to use `reqwest::Result<T>` instead of `std::io::Result<T>`. This is because the error being generated is of type `reqwest::Error`, not `std::io::Error`. Here's the corrected version:

```rust
// Add necessary imports
use reqwest::{Client, Error, Response, Result};

async fn fetch(url: &str) -> Result<Response> {
    let client = Client::new();

    let response = client.get(url).send().await?;

    Ok(response)
}
```

This code assumes that you have the `reqwest` crate as a dependency in your `Cargo.toml` file. If not, add it:

```toml
[dependencies]
reqwest = "0.11"
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] } 
```

